# candidate T29 -- the compact raw-message carrier (a WALL removal)
#   The raw message becomes u32 WORDS: RawRq32(Vec<u32>) / RawVec32,
#   plus _32 consumers (commit_streamed_32, honest_z_from_raw_32,
#   carrier_{from,decomp,commit}_from_raw_32, honest_compute_{v,resp}
#   _from_raw_32) and chain_open switched to take it.
# This run is a GUARD, not a speed claim. T29 only ADDS items to ring,
#   linalg, commit and quadeval (chain_open's signature changes, and it
#   is EXCLUDED from benching); every row measured here is code that is
#   byte-identical in both arms, so the question is whether adding the
#   items perturbed the codegen of the ones already there. Nothing may
#   read slower.
# The _32 items' own rows cannot be registered yet: a new row needs the
#   item in the genesis crate too, and the genesis appends are PARKED
#   for this run (an unstamped genesis item fails check-genesis, and the
#   stamp records the content commit's sha). Same chicken-and-egg as
#   Change 8; same resolution.
# Measured at the pin (VmHWM, in-process, logs/runs/pin-profile-20260918
#   -{baseline,t29}.log): peak 12573 -> 8477 MiB, -4096 MiB / -32.6%.
#   Time: commitment -1.8%, honest_compute_v -0.7%, rounds -0.3%,
#   chain_verify -1.4%, honest_compute_resp +8.4% (it makes TWO passes
#   over the message, so it pays the expansion twice; T28 removes one).
# quiet: idle=99% sustained over 3 samples
